  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/C1/). VERDICT: CURRENT, numbers worse, one premise wrong. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/selection_index.sqlite = 3,385,262,080 B (3.15 GiB; 2.3 GB at filing), page_size 4096, 826,480 pages, auto_vacuum 0, freelist 1,313; fincore 4.3 MB resident (cold again). No VACUUM/prune anywhere (selection_index.py:392 says 'nothing prunes it'). EXPLAIN (read-only): block WHERE path=? -> covering autoindex; test_block WHERE path=? AND name=? -> test_block_by_block; a full covering-index SCAN only on SELECT DISTINCT test_id FROM test_block (touching_test_files :430, speakable_test_files :452 - the opt-in narrow path). So 'missing index -> full scans' is wrong: every point query is indexed; the random reads are B-tree page access on the per-run fold (DELETE ... WHERE test_id=? + executemany INSERT into two B-trees, smart-test:702/1969) and point lookups over a file nothing compacts (about 1 GB/month). open_index (:125-126) sets no PRAGMA (no mmap_size/cache_size). Title re-scoped. ROOT CAUSE: append-only index with no compaction, so cold-cache cost scales with total size, not the query's working set (singleton, CI tooling family). Status unchanged."  # 7ce1
- op: discuss  # 7ddf
  at: '2026-11-13T05:31:38Z'  # 7ddf
  by: agent  # 7ddf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7ddf
  clock: 4  # 7ddf
  nonce: 7ddf  # 7ddf
  message: "PLAN 2026-11-13 (owner-approved in session: \"record the plan on WI-romam and implement it\"). MEASURED TODAY on dev d58dd736f1: selection_index.sqlite = 3,838,394,368 B, 937,108 pages, freelist 99,803 (10.6%). test_block = 4,474,443 rows and, with its two indexes, 3.1 GB of the 3.6 GB in use (dbstat: PK autoindex 1,305 MB, table 1,114 MB, test_block_by_block 709 MB). Average row = test_id 125 chars + absolute path 92 + block name 19, stored in the table and again in the PK index. 34,302 distinct tests, 13,147 distinct files, 243,444 blocks. Stale rows are NOT the size: 4 test ids belong to deleted test files, 0 test_block rows lack a block row. So pruning gains nothing and VACUUM gains about 10%; the size is repeated text. NEW SINCE 11-12: narrowing is default (WI-zirus), and each narrowed run does two full covering-index scans of test_block (touching_test_files, speakable_test_files); warm they take 0.8 s and 0.5 s; the docstring's premise 'a few tens of thousands of rows' is false (4.47 M). STEPS: (1) time a narrowed run cold (evict the file with posix_fadvise DONTNEED; cap 15 min) as the before figure. (2) integer-id schema: test, file and block rows stored once, pair table of two integers; PRAGMA user_version marks the format so an old file is never read as an empty index; public function signatures unchanged. (3) convert the existing file, no test run: write a new file, swap it in, under smart-test's lock, automatically when new code opens an old-format file; keep the old file until step 5 passes. (4) the two narrowing queries become indexed lookups (by-block index for 'which tests touch these files'; the tests table for 'which files are fully measured'). (5) prove equivalence: row counts, then select and narrow output identical on old and new files for a sample of recent commits; repo tests for the conversion, an interrupted conversion, and an old-format file opened by new code. (6) time cold again; close only if coverage-select finishes under 1 minute from a cold cache (this item's acceptance). OUT OF SCOPE: pruning (4 stale ids); making narrowing remove more (refusal rules and the whole-file keep set are owner decisions)."  # 7ddf
